# Round XXVII Track D (Core #12 axis coverage — collection-kind axis):
# `HashSet[T].enumerate()` in a `for` loop is a check-time REJECT, mirror of
# the Set fixture. Same rationale: `.enumerate()` is `Iterator[T]`-only per
# `lib/std/iter.gg:307/814`, and HashSet impls `Iterable[T]`. Pre-D27 same
# silent-zero-output miscompile as Set (both hit `lower_for_enumerate` with
# a Vector-shaped `iter.Field(2)` read against the hash-table layout).
#
# The Set + HashSet pair pins both cells of the collection-kind axis so a
# future arm that re-adds only ONE of the two silently regresses the other.
int main():
    HashSet[int] h = {1, 2, 3}
    # Rejected at check-time: `.enumerate()` requires Iterator[T]; HashSet
    # is Iterable[T] only. Fix: `h.iter().enumerate()`.
    for i, x in h.enumerate():
        print(f"{i}={x}")
    return 0
